# <%~ it.instance.name || it.instance.slug %>: Hire Record
<%
  /* The permanent file: every module in the definition, in the order the process ran. Sections
     are grouped by stage rather than by module so the document reads as a chronology — which is
     how anyone coming to it later will read it.
     This is the only artefact carrying `contract.elapsed` and `open-questions.process-gaps`.
     Both are optional and both are where this definition's real value accumulates: one measures
     the process against its own stated fifteen days, the other records where it did not hold
     up. See the current-state note in v1's definition.yaml.

     There are no approval sections anywhere in this record. Each of the four stages was signed
     off by a merged pull request, and that history is a better account of who approved what
     than a field restating it would be.

     v2 (#90): named from the candidate alone, not the start date — this document is filed once
     and kept, and a moved start date recorded in `contract.start-date-changes` shouldn't rename
     it (definition.yaml's `filename:`). `selection.preferred-candidate` split into
     `candidate-name` and `rationale`; `engagement.term` is a new optional field beside
     `engagement.type`; `contract.start-date` is now a date, formatted here with
     `formatDate()`.

     v3 (#157): Provisioning prints the new `identity.user-id`, `device.standard` and
     `device.build-notes`, and `access.outstanding` under its new title. The readiness
     confirmation is gone: readiness is the ready-to-start sign-off itself. */
